  "_instructions": {
    "title": "How to Add Real Battle Maps",
    "steps": [
      "1. Find CC0/Public Domain battle maps from sources like:",
      "   - reddit.com/r/battlemaps (filter for free/CC0)",
      "   - 2minutetabletop.com (some free maps)",
      "   - dungeondraft.net community",
      "   - inkarnate.com (free tier)",
      "",
      "2. Place map images in: static/assets/maps/",
      "   - Use web-optimized formats (JPG for photos, PNG for transparency)",
      "   - Recommended resolution: 1400-2400px for the longest side",
      "   - Name format: category-description-number.jpg",
      "",
      "3. Create thumbnails (optional but recommended):",
      "   - 300x300px or similar small size",
      "   - Name format: [mapname]-thumb.jpg",
      "",
      "4. Update this maps.json file:",
      "   - Copy an existing map entry",
      "   - Update all fields (id, name, filename, etc.)",
      "   - Set isPlaceholder to false",
      "   - Add proper attribution if required",
      "",
      "5. The MapBrowser component will automatically load your maps!",
      "",
      "Note: Placeholder maps show a message in the browser to add real images."
    ]
  }
